{'symbol': 'HD', 'date': '2019-11-19 09:30:00', 'title': 'The Home Depot Posts Q3 EPS Of $2.53', 'text': "THE HOME DEPOT ANNOUNCES THIRD QUARTER RESULTS; UPDATES FISCAL YEAR 2019 GUIDANCE.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE $2.53.Q3 SALES $27.2 BILLION VERSUS REFINITIV IBES ESTIMATE OF $27.53 BILLION.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE ESTIMATE $2.52 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.SEES FY 2019 SALES UP ABOUT 1.8 PERCENT.EXPECTS ITS FISCAL 2019 SALES TO GROW BY APPROXIMATELY 1.8 PERCENT.COMPARABLE SALES FOR Q3 OF FISCAL 2019 WERE POSITIVE 3.6 PERCENT.EXPECTS ITS FISCAL 2019 COMP SALES FOR COMPARABLE 52-WEEK PERIOD TO INCREASE ABOUT 3.5%.COMPARABLE SALES IN U.S. WERE POSITIVE 3.8 PERCENT IN QUARTER.REAFFIRMED ITS DILUTED EARNINGS-PER-SHARE GUIDANCE FOR YEAR.FY EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $10.13, REVENUE VIEW $110.76 BILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.HOME DEPOT - SOME BENEFITS FROM ONE HOME DEPOT STRATEGIC INVESTMENTS ANTICIPATED FOR FISCAL 2019 WILL TAKE LONGER TO REALIZE THAN INITIAL ASSUMPTIONS.HOME DEPOT SAYS SALES IN QUARTER WERE BELOW CO'S EXPECTATIONS DRIVEN BY TIMING OF SOME BENEFITS ASSOCIATED WITH ONE HOME DEPOT INVESTMENTS."}
{'symbol': 'HD', 'date': '2019-11-19 22:30:00', 'title': 'The Home Depot, Inc. Reaffirms Earnings Guidance for 2019', 'text': "The Home Depot, Inc. reaffirmed earnings guidance for 2019. The company is updating fiscal 2019 sales guidance, and the company is reaffirming fiscal 2019 earnings-per-share guidance. The Company expects its fiscal 2019 sales to grow by approximately 1.8% and comp sales for the comparable 52-week period to increase approximately 3.5%. This compares to the Company's prior fiscal 2019 sales growth guidance of 2.3% and comp sales growth of 4.0%. The Company reaffirmed its diluted earnings-per-share guidance for the year and expects diluted earnings-per-share growth of approximately 3.1% from fiscal 2018 to $10.03."}
{'symbol': 'HPQ', 'date': '2019-11-19 22:30:00', 'title': 'HP Provides Information to Shareholders', 'text': "On November 19, 2019, HP Inc. announced that it has rejected $US33bn ($48.4bn) takeover offer from Xerox Corp as too low, but it was interested in discussing a deal to combine with its smaller rival. The Company stated that it recognized the benefits of consolidation and was ‘open to exploring a potential combination with Xerox’. In addition, the Company stated in its letter it urged Xerox to let it perform additional due diligence so it could better understand Xerox's recent revenue declines and analyze potential cost savings from a combination, which Xerox has pegged at $US2bn."}
